<Markdown id="wp_rend_s01">*The half sheets are on the corner of your desk. The clock says minute {{Math.round(10 + sum([@wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code, @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code, @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code, @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code, @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code]) / 60)}}. The exit ticket was at thirty.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s02" when="10 + sum([@wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code, @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code, @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code, @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code, @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code]) / 60 &lt;= 33">*Ten minutes. "Draw and label what you think is happening under the ice." Silent. You sort the sheets at your desk while they line up for specials, into three piles for Lesson 2.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s03" when="10 + sum([@wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code, @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code, @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code, @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code, @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code]) / 60 &gt; 33 &amp;&amp; 10 + sum([@wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code, @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code, @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code, @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code, @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code]) / 60 &lt;= 37">*"Just draw it. Labels if you have time." Two children are still drawing when you collect. You sort the sheets after they line up, into three piles for Lesson 2.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s04" when="10 + sum([@wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code, @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code, @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code, @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code, @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code]) / 60 &gt; 37 &amp;&amp; 10 + sum([@wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code, @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code, @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code, @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code, @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code]) / 60 &lt;= 41">*"Quick sketch. Two minutes." The bell goes while Amani is still drawing. You sort them at four o'clock, and most of them are a lake with a line across it.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s05" when="10 + sum([@wp_ra1.code, @wp_ra2.code, @wp_rb1.code, @wp_rb2.code, @wp_rb3.code, @wp_rc1.code, @wp_rc2.code, @wp_rd1.code, @wp_rd2.code, @wp_re1.code, @wp_re2.code, @wp_rf1.code, @wp_rf2.code, @wp_rg1.code, @wp_rg2.code, @wp_rg3.code, @wp_rh1.code, @wp_rh2.code]) / 60 &gt; 41">*The bell. The half sheets are still in their stack, twenty-four copies and three spare. Lesson 2's groups come from memory: Marcus, Aaliyah, Bri, Darnell{{(@wp_rb1.value === 'take_up') ? ', Kenny' : ''}}{{(@wp_rb2.value === 'ask_room') ? ', Thuy, Espy' : ''}}{{(@wp_rc1.value === 'hand_to_room') ? ', Espy' : ''}}{{(@wp_rd1.value === 'jaylen') ? ', Jaylen' : ''}}{{(@wp_rd2.value === 'keisha') ? ', Keisha' : ''}}{{(@wp_rh1.value === 'together') ? ', Diego' : ''}}. Diego goes in whichever group has a space.*</Markdown>

<!-- Per-child placement and the reason, from ep-end.md section 3. For the
     builder and for Piotr; not rendered.

     - Marcus: pile 1 always. He has stood on the ice and held the fish.
     - Aaliyah: pile 1 always. Her mother gave her the mechanism in the kitchen.
       What the lesson did to her is in the corner of the sheet, not in the pile.
     - Bri: pile 1 always. She had the question; what is written under the ice varies.
     - Diego: pile 1 always. He has seen ice on top of a cup. Whether anything is
       written under it varies.
     - Amani: pile 1 always. He draws better than he writes.
     - Darnell: pile 1 if the room reasoned about floating in front of him (C_ROOM,
       B_BRIDGED, G_WAITED); otherwise pile 2, the fish drawn on the ice beside the
       skaters, because recall gave him three words and nothing to draw from.
     - Thuy: pile 1 if she predicted or heard the bridge (G_WAITED, B_BRIDGED,
       C_ROOM); otherwise pile 2.
     - Espy: pile 1 if she relayed Diego's cup (C_ROOM); otherwise pile 2.
     - Kenny: pile 3 if the room did pipes (B_ROOM): he drew his building with the
       water coming down the stairs. Otherwise pile 2.
     - Jaylen: pile 1 with a jar in the margin if E_CHARTED; pile 3 if E_RUN, the
       jar and the string and no lake; otherwise pile 2.
     - Keisha: pile 1 if F_RULE or F_CHARTED, with "two cups" in the margin;
       otherwise pile 2.
-->

