<Markdown id="wp_rend_m20">**The chart, as it stays up all unit.** NOTICE: the lake is frozen · people are skating · it's winter · you can't see the fish. WONDER: how thick is the ice? · is anybody fishing?</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s21" when="@wp_ra2.value === 'chart'">*"cold comes from the sky (Marcus)", in blue, under NOTICE. It stays up until February. Lesson 6 is about where the lake's heat goes, and it goes up, not down.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s22" when="(@wp_rb1.value === 'park') || (@wp_rb2.value === 'name_it')">*"Aaliyah: pipes busted in the freeze. L3", in blue, under WONDER.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s23" when="@wp_rb3.value === 'bridge'">*"same ice: busts a pipe, sits on a lake?", in blue, under WONDER.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s24" when="@wp_rc1.value === 'hold'">*"why does ice float? (Bri)", starred, "L3" in the margin.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s25" when="@wp_re1.value === 'park' || @wp_re2.value === 'distinction'">*"rock candy: a change, not our change (Jaylen)", small, in the corner.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s26" when="@wp_rf1.value === 'park' || @wp_rf2.value === 'chart_rule' || @wp_rf2.value === 'ask_ocean'">*"does the ocean freeze? two cups (Keisha)", under WONDER.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s27" when="@wp_rg3.value === 'rewrite'">*On the board, under the three words: "ice takes up more room". Nothing underlined.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s28" when="!(@wp_rg3.value === 'rewrite')">*On the board, under the three words: "ice is lighter, it floats", underlined twice.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s29" when="@wp_ra1.value === 'praise_next'">*Not on either surface: Marcus's ice fishing.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_s30" when="@wp_rb1.value === 'redirect'">*Not on either surface: Aaliyah's pipes.*</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_m31">## Your choices: what they made possible, and what they cost</Markdown>

<Markdown id="wp_rend_m32">
There was no path through that launch that took up every child and still made the exit ticket, so this isn't about whether you got it right. It's about the reasoning behind your choices of who to call on and whose ideas to take up.

Look at the clock, the strip, and the pile. Then, in a few sentences:

- name **one choice that made something possible**: for which child, or for the science;
- say **what it cost**: in minutes, in another child's turn, or in the plan;
- and say whether you'd **make that trade again**, and why.

Name at least one child and one minute.
</Markdown>

<TextArea id="wp_replay_reflection" rows="5"
          placeholder="When I... it made it possible for... It cost... I would / wouldn't make that trade again because..." />
